<description>&lt;p&gt;Iraqi security forces have moved troops to Jurf al-Sakhr and Jurf al-Nasr and are preparing a senior meeting on oil-smuggling investigations, while the prime minister Al-Zaidi has ordered an inquiry into smuggling in Kirkuk and ordered the special force and energy police to target pipelines. Kataib Hezbollah has rejected the oil probe findings, accused the prime minister of yielding to US and Gulf pressure, and faces a deadline to vacate the area, with Al-Zaidi threatening force to assert control. The government has banned Telegram for regulatory violations and arrested five people for impersonating a prosecutor. 396 battle-related deaths were recorded in 2024, according to UCDP.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Machine-written from the linked sources, checked for figures and names not in them.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.?oc=5&quot;&gt;Al Jazeera&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.?oc=5&quot;&gt;Al Jazeera&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.?oc=5&quot;&gt;Al Jazeera&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiqwFBVV95cUxObl9vMTVVaFdVTGt0TjhFYVJNNEdEMWkxRGpSOTJXYkZOeFhNMmEtaFFVTGZFNlN4ZFBVeDN0aWpfMTRBb0pLVGt5cDM5N010S0NCSWlOMUlOLU5xNGFyNUhQUk5COHVLSWtTblRoVzNLeWFGdmVOeEF2NkZXd0EybUJyS2tVNDhRNHVIazFZQ3RpdGw0Nlh6Sjc4LVdpRFpqR01PSXZfaUlNek0?oc=5&quot;&gt;Kurdistan24&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMijgFBVV95cUxOcGpBUkVMVmRpclFudDJZWmxITGNKcnJMM1pGUjJsTVk0S0RZaHh5TWtNLWRwTU5CSmhoakRNQ2RWeE82RjJ0a0VYeFhxRmc2ejEtLUtVXzBTbGtRN2lHeUdtQnNhdWRRXzlBQmFLTk1wUVhhakVjTzc1TUtqTXZGOGZIbnZjbF9LYkQxVjB3?oc=5&quot;&gt;The New Arab&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiyAFBVV95cUxOSG9kdWFyYmlhVE5VNjUySHFMTDFHekx5VnRxcWVZRVNWVVNGM25sc1ZlZEsxTGJMZzlJbVVMX2JPbjQ1VG9CZDhvajhCblRZc0haVkQyQVk5aFhEWF9Rb28zT3ZzaTRTeUQwNEFDR1RuRGFQVUFoVy1QeThJM2FkVElCOXIxcjkwQV8yMlRjWVZVbDZfLXhLb3dWaklXUDZINHRGVkE2aXYzXzhlcjVucS1LSF9SUHBvcEtk